  using 1 OpenMP thread(s) per MPI task
# samQEq host-vs-device throughput benchmark: native SPC-FQ water (paper Section sec:water),
# base.data (512 molecules, equilibrated by in.equil) replicated REP^3 times.
#   -var REP n      replication per axis (2 -> 12,288 atoms; 4 -> 98,304; 6 -> 331,776; 8 -> 786,432)
#   -var NSTEP n    timed steps
#   -var DEV 0|1    1 = `fix_modify chg devsolve on` (KOKKOS binary only; the device charge solve)
#   -var ASPC 0|1   1 = `fix_modify chg aspc 2` (predictor-corrector); 0 = full solve every step
#   -var DUMP 0|1   1 = write per-atom charges at step 0 and at the last step (agreement check)
#   -var TAG s      label for the dump files
variable        REP   index 2
variable        NSTEP index 200
variable        DEV   index 0
variable        ASPC  index 0
variable        DUMP  index 0
variable        TAG   index run
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
special_bonds   lj/coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
read_data       base.data
